# Build output --------------------------------------------------------------
build/
dist/
*.spec

# ...but the browser edition's assets live in docs/dist and MUST be published:
# the page fetches the packed Python sources and the openpyxl wheel from beside
# itself.  Hiding them breaks the live site, not just the build.
!docs/dist/

# web/dist is the same set of files before they are copied to the site.  The page
# builder reads them and the browser suite asserts they match src/, so a fresh
# clone without them can do neither -- which is exactly how CI first failed here.
!web/dist/

# Release archives ----------------------------------------------------------
# The ZIPs are attached to a GitHub Release, not committed: 390 MB of binaries
# in git history would be permanent and would not help anyone.
release/

# Python --------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Test and tooling output ---------------------------------------------------
# Staged only while the browser test runs.
web/sample.adi
*.xlsx
!samples/sample_output.xlsx
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Generated fixtures --------------------------------------------------------
# The six anonymised platform exports under tests/fixtures/adi/ ARE committed:
# they are the most valuable regression fixtures in the project.  Regenerate
# them from the originals with:  python tests/make_fixtures.py <folder>
tests/fixtures/adi/*.tmp

# Editors and OS ------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
